Suggests: phi-mosquitto
Description: MQTT endpoint transport for phi-core
 phi as an MQTT endpoint: the tenant's devices, channels, rooms and scenes
 published on a broker, and commands accepted there, so Home Assistant,
 openHAB, ioBroker, Node-RED and plain scripts can consume a phi box without
 speaking phi's own WebSocket protocol.
 .
 A transport plugin for phi-core, hosted out of process by phi-transport-host
 (config /etc/phi/@1/transports/mqtt.json, state under
 /var/lib/phi/@1/transports/mqtt/state). On the box it logs in to the box
 broker (phi-mosquitto) with an account phi-hostd mints for it; a broker on
 another machine is configured in mqtt.json.
